## Blocker: the remaining work is the L-card implementation, not missing evidence

The card is a single artefact (one `.epe`, one object count), so a partial graph was **not** staged:
`Working/Entity/` does not exist, `Builds/bm-003/` does not exist, and `Tools/scripts/bm_entity.py`
does not exist. A half-built entity graph is worse than none — the next run would have to guess which
objects were planned — and an invented object would break R4.

What is left, concretely (all inputs are on disk now):

| step | state |
|---|---|
| 1 — 19 `CPartProp` inserts | specified: clone a node, set `<object id>`, `name`, `name_hash = hash_jenkins(name)` (**verified 5/5** on shipped `CPartProp` values), `part_index` from B-04's module (42…60); proven to survive `--i` |
| 2 — weapon component + `SWeaponPoint`s | specified: template = the armed APC's `CBulletWeaponBase` (schema recorded below); values from T-11's carrier rows and `SOCKETS_JC3.json` |
| 3 — 16 `SVehicleLight` rows | inputs on disk (`t14_lights.json` `rows`/`custom`/`parts`/`light_parts`); 22 `SVehicleLight` objects already in the graph, so the member set is copyable |
| 4 — 77 interaction transforms | input on disk (`t9_interaction.json` `objects`, `band_m` [0.05, 0.30]); needs the id → `.epe` object mapping |
| 5 — root `health`/`invulnerable` | input on disk (`t10_damage_edits.json`), root already carries `health` 100 / `invulnerable` 0 |
| build + Done checks | `bm-003` from `bm-002`, `.toc` patch for the `.epe`, then the three Done commands |

